---
name: Parse, assemble, and map in stages
description: |
  Runs the steps of the normalizer one by one. The parsed records and the
  assembled event are available for routing or inspection before the OCSF
  mapping. Here, a failed login of an unknown SSH user maps to an OCSF
  Authentication event.
---

from {line: "node=bastion.example type=USER_LOGIN msg=audit(1767225601.000:7022): pid=2311 uid=0 auid=4294967295 ses=4294967295 subj=unconfined msg='op=login acct=28696E76616C6964207573657229 exe=\"/usr/sbin/sshd\" hostname=? addr=203.0.113.77 terminal=sshd res=failed'"}
auditd::parse line, record
auditd::assemble line, record
auditd::ocsf::map record, ocsf
this = ocsf_derive(ocsf)
